@startuml
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #0B7A75
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F4FAF9
  BorderColor #0B7A75
  FontColor #14312F
  FontSize 13
}

title The Gate decides nothing: it collects and passes; the UniversalNavigator proves every arrival from the registry

[*] --> AtGate

state "Request at the Gate" as AtGate
state "Handed to the UniversalNavigator" as AtNav
state "Matched against the live registry" as Resolve
state "The proof the route names is verified" as Prove
state "Refused" as Refused #FDF2F2
state "Dispatched to the subscribed tool" as Dispatched #F2F9F4

AtGate --> AtNav : collect the session token, the HTTP head,\nand the POST/GET parameters — each if present.\nThe Gate verifies nothing; it knows only transport.

AtNav --> Resolve : the UniversalNavigator is the only\nnode that accepts external traffic

Resolve --> Refused : the arrival matches\nno route — **refuse**
Resolve --> Prove : a route matches; its call_type\nnames the proof required

Prove --> Refused : proof missing or invalid — **refuse**
Prove --> Dispatched : proof holds — dispatch by subscription

Refused --> [*]
Dispatched --> [*]

note right of Prove
  <b>Proof by call type (from the registry route)</b>
  static_witness  →  none — log the frame pop, decide nothing
  client_sessioned  →  session_token — signed, per-hop nonce
  third_party_callback  →  api_key — a credential we keep in the vault
  internal_callback  →  our_signature — we signed the dispatch out

  tool_to_tool is internal: relayed tool to tool through the
  UniversalNavigatorProxy, and never reaches the Gate.
end note

note as OpenQs #FFF9E6
  <b>Open architectural questions — recorded, not resolved here</b>
  • <b>Dispatch location.</b> This diagram places dispatch at the
    UniversalNavigator and keeps the Gate transport-only. REQ-B-001
    is authoritative; if its text instead places dispatch on the Gate,
    requirement and design disagree and the requirement governs.
    (ledger N36 → resolve in C6)
  • <b>Session issuance.</b> Where a client_sessioned token is minted is
    undecided: an unauthenticated op on the Gate (one entrance, no op
    exempt weakened) vs a separate endpoint (every op authenticated, one
    more entrance). Minting confers nothing; resuming a session is a
    defect wherever it lives. (ledger N15 → resolve in C5)
end note

@enduml
